    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d56">

                <pb facs="0178" n="108" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg108"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Inquiry files</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Dr. S. E.
                            Mezes to the Treasurer of the Inquiry</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Miller</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi>
                        </placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-15">October 15,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Miller</hi>: After an official conference Colonel House has given instructions that the
                    work of the Inquiry should be speeded up and has authorized a monthly
                    expenditure for this and subsequent months for the Inquiry proper of $25,000 if
                    necessary, with the understanding that additional employees shall be taken on
                    only until the time when the official force proceeds to the Conference, except
                    in such cases as it may prove quite impossible to obtain satisfactory appointees
                    without offering them a longer term.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">S. E. Mezes</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
